```apex
public class ContactDomainService {

    private static final Integer QUERY_BATCH_SIZE = 1000;

    public static Map<String, List<Contact>> groupByEmailDomain(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        Map<String, List<Contact>> result = new Map<String, List<Contact>>();

        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        List<Contact> allContacts = new List<Contact>();
        List<Id> idList = new List<Id>(accountIds);
        Integer total = idList.size();

        // Chunk to respect the 1000-item SOQL IN governor limit
        for (Integer i = 0; i < total; i += QUERY_BATCH_SIZE) {
            Integer end = Math.min(i + QUERY_BATCH_SIZE, total);
            List<Id> batch = idList.sublist(i, end);

            // SOQL in Apex automatically enforces the running user's sharing rules
            List<Contact> contacts = [
                SELECT Id, Email, AccountId
                FROM Contact
                WHERE AccountId IN :batch
            ];

            allContacts.addAll(contacts);
        }

        // Group contacts by lower-cased email domain
        for (Contact c : allContacts) {
            if (String.isBlank(c.Email)) {
                continue;
            }

            String email = c.Email.trim();
            Integer atIdx = email.lastIndexOf('@');
            if (atIdx < 0 || atIdx == email.length() - 1) {
                continue;
            }

            String domain = email.substring(atIdx + 1).toLowerCase();
            if (String.isBlank(domain)) {
                continue;
            }

            if (!result.containsKey(domain)) {
                result.put(domain, new List<Contact>());
            }
            result.get(domain).add(c);
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Null / empty input** | Early return of an empty map before any DML/SOQL. |
| **Bulk safety** | The `Set<Id>` is converted to a `List` and queried in chunks of 1000 to stay within the SOQL `IN`-clause governor limit. A caller passing 50 000 account IDs will issue 50 queries instead of hitting the 1000 cap. |
| **Sharing** | The query is a SOQL statement inside Apex, which Salesforce automatically filters by the running user's object and row-level sharing. No `WITH SECURITY_ENFORCED` is needed for a plain `SELECT` (it is a query, not a DML). |
| **Required fields** | The `SELECT` explicitly retrieves `Id`, `Email`, and `AccountId` — the three fields the contract requires. |
| **Domain extraction** | Splits on the **last** `@` (handles addresses like `user+tag@example.com`), lower-cases the result, and skips entries that have no `@` or an empty domain part. |
| **Case normalisation** | `toLowerCase()` ensures `Jane@Example.COM` and `jane@example.com` land in the same bucket. |

