```apex
public class AccountOnboardingService {

    public static List<Account> createAccountsWithContacts(Map<String, List<String>> contactLastNamesByAccountName) {
        if (contactLastNamesByAccountName == null || contactLastNamesByAccountName.isEmpty()) {
            return new List<Account>();
        }

        fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork uow = new fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork();

        // Phase 1 – queue all Accounts, then insert them so their Ids are populated
        List<Account> accounts = new List<Account>();
        for (String accountName : contactLastNamesByAccountName.keySet()) {
            Account acc = new Account(Name = accountName);
            accounts.add(acc);
            uow.addSObject(acc);
        }
        uow.commitWork();

        // Phase 2 – queue all Contacts with the now-resolved AccountId, then insert
        List<Contact> contacts = new List<Contact>();
        for (Account acc : accounts) {
            List<String> lastNames = contactLastNamesByAccountName.get(acc.Name);
            if (lastNames != null) {
                for (String lastName : lastNames) {
                    Contact con = new Contact(LastName = lastName, AccountId = acc.Id);
                    contacts.add(con);
                    uow.addSObject(con);
                }
            }
        }

        if (!contacts.isEmpty()) {
            uow.commitWork();
        }

        return accounts;
    }
}
```

**How it works / design notes**

| Concern | How it's addressed |
|---|---|
| **Single work-unit instance** | One `fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork` is created and used for every write in the method. No raw DML is issued. |
| **Parent → child FK resolution** | Two `commitWork()` calls are needed because the `Contact.AccountId` cannot be known until the `Account` rows exist. The first commit inserts the Accounts and populates their `Id` fields in memory; the second commit inserts the Contacts. This is the canonical fflib pattern for parent–child creation. |
| **Null / empty map** | Guard at the top returns an empty list immediately—no work-unit is even constructed. |
| **Bulk safety (hundreds of contacts)** | `fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork` batches all queued SObjects of the same type into a single `INSERT` per commit call, so the SOQL/DML governor limits are respected regardless of how many entries are in the map. |
| **Return value** | The in-memory `Account` objects have their `Id` populated by the first `commitWork()`, so the returned list is immediately usable. |

