**How it works**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| Skip welcome task for imported contacts | `TAFUtility.bypassAction(c, …)` marks each SObject *instance* so TAF skips that action when the trigger fires for it. |
| Phone formatting still runs | Only `TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask` is bypassed; `TA_Contact_FormatPhone` is untouched and executes normally in the before-insert trigger. |
| Single DML | `insert contacts;` is one bulk DML statement. |
| Bypass inactive after the call | The per-SObject bypass is keyed to the specific instance references. Contacts created later in the same transaction are different objects, so TAF sees no bypass flag on them and fires the welcome task as usual. No explicit "un-bypass" call is needed. |

